-- @sync FUNCTION SUSPENDS -------------------------------------- main.kl  K1402

This function is marked `@sync`, a promise that it never waits, but it calls something that can suspend. The chain of calls shows where.

2│ fn present(fs: Fs) -> Bool => fs.exists(path"notes.txt")
      ^^^^^^^ `present` calls `exists` (suspends)

Help: Remove the waiting call from this function, or remove `@sync` if the function really needs to wait (callers that rely on it will then be reported).

